# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GymOS — committed development defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file IS tracked in git, deliberately. Both values below are public by
# design: Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable into the client bundle,
# so the anon key is already served to every visitor's browser on page load.
# Committing it changes nothing about its exposure and removes the manual
# setup step in a fresh Codespace.
#
# The anon key carries `role: anon`. It grants no data access on its own —
# every table is protected by row-level security, and the owner cockpit RPCs
# additionally re-assert tenant + role from the verified JWT. Confirmed:
# an unauthenticated REST read against /members returns [].
#
# NEVER add to this file:
#   * DATABASE_URL or any Postgres connection string (superuser; RLS does not
#     apply to it)
#   * SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (bypasses RLS entirely)
#   * POOLER_URL used by the fixture-reset scripts
# Those belong in .env.local (git-ignored) or in CI secrets.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://udswbuuhrrfmwtkearbl.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InVkc3didXVocnJmbXd0a2VhcmJsIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODYwOTIyMDUsImV4cCI6MjEwMTY2ODIwNX0.QZHhwNosAZ8ClF6To1jI5rrZJhW4am7rge8SiwWUsac
